Ansible Installation & Setup

Today I set up the Ansible environment, which is the first hands-on step toward real automation.

A correct setup is critical—most Ansible issues come from SSH or environment misconfiguration.

🔹 Install Ansible on Linux
Ansible is installed only on the control node.

Common steps include:
Update system packages
Install Ansible using package manager
Verify installation
Ansible runs best on Linux-based systems.

🔹 SSH Key-Based Authentication
Ansible uses SSH to connect to managed nodes.

Key-based authentication:
Removes password prompts
Is more secure than passwords
Enables automation without manual input
This is mandatory for smooth Ansible execution.

🔹 Verify Connectivity
Before running playbooks, connectivity must be checked:
Ensure SSH access works
Test communication with hosts
Confirm permissions
This avoids failures during automation runs.

🔹 ansible --version
This command helps to:
Confirm Ansible installation
Check Ansible version
Verify Python dependency
It’s the first command to run after setup.

🔥 3-Line Takeaway
Setup enables automation.
 SSH builds trust.
 Verification avoids failure.
